(PROTOCOL CS-2026-88 | CLINICAL STUDY REPORT) Tj
T* (--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T* (SECTION 1: EXECUTIVE SUMMARY & OBJECTIVES) Tj
T* (--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (1.1 Study Background & Rationale) Tj
T* (Impaired stratum corneum barrier function and dysregulated sebum excretion are cardinal) Tj
T* (pathophysiological hallmarks of mild-to-moderate acne vulgaris and dehydrated facial skin.) Tj
T* (Formula B-88 is an advanced topical formulation containing biomimetic ceramides,) Tj
T* (hyaluronic acid multi-molecular complex, and 2% zinc PCA.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (1.2 Primary Efficacy Objectives) Tj
T* (1. To evaluate quantitative change in stratum corneum hydration over a 14-day duration.) Tj
T* (2. To measure reduction in facial sebum excretion rate \(ug/cm2\) on the forehead and T-zone.) Tj
T* (3. To determine reduction in inflammatory and non-inflammatory acne lesion counts.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (1.3 Secondary Safety Objectives) Tj
T* (1. To determine cutaneous tolerance, erythema index, and adverse reaction profile.) Tj
T* (2. To verify transepidermal water loss \(TEWL\) reduction as a barrier integrity surrogate.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Page 2 of 8) Tj
ET
endstream
>>
