(PROTOCOL CS-2026-88 | CLINICAL STUDY REPORT) Tj
T* (--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T* (SECTION 2: STUDY DESIGN & METHODOLOGY) Tj
T* (--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (2.1 Study Methodology) Tj
T* (Double-blind, randomized, placebo-controlled clinical trial with parallel-group design.) Tj
T* (Eligible subjects were randomly allocated \(1:1\) to twice-daily topical application of) Tj
T* (Formula B-88 active serum or vehicle placebo for an uninterrupted 14-day study period.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (2.2 Blinding & Randomization) Tj
T* (Both active serum and vehicle control were packaged in identical opaque airless dispensers) Tj
T* (bearing unique randomization codes generated via permuted block algorithm \(block size of 4\).) Tj
T* (Both study participants and investigative dermatologists remained blinded throughout.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (2.3 Inclusion & Exclusion Criteria) Tj
T* (- Healthy male and female subjects aged 18 to 55 years.) Tj
T* (- Presence of mild-to-moderate facial dehydration \(Corneometer baseline < 40 a.u.\).) Tj
T* (- Baseline casual sebum level >= 150 ug/cm2 \(Sebumeter SM 815\).) Tj
T* (- Minimum of 15 facial inflammatory/comedonal acne lesions at screening.) Tj
T* (- Exclusion: Concomitant topical/systemic retinoids or corticosteroids within 30 days.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Page 3 of 8) Tj
ET
endstream
