(PROTOCOL CS-2026-88 | CLINICAL STUDY REPORT) Tj
T* (--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T* (SECTION 6: STATISTICAL RESULTS & QUANTITATIVE CLINICAL ENDPOINTS) Tj
T* (--------------------------------------------------------------------------------) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Table 2.1: Quantitative Clinical Endpoints at Day 14) Tj
T* (=================================================================================================) Tj
T* (Endpoint Parameter                  Baseline Mean \(SD\)  Day 14 Mean \(SD\)  Mean Delta \(%\)   p-value) Tj
T* (=================================================================================================) Tj
T* (Stratum Corneum Hydration \(%\)       31.4 \(4.2\)          61.0 \(5.1\)        +94.2%           p < 0.001) Tj
T* (Inflammatory Acne Lesion Count      25.0 \(3.8\)          8.0 \(2.1\)         -68.0%           p < 0.001) Tj
T* (Casual Sebum Excretion \(ug/cm2\)     188.2 \(22.5\)        108.2 \(16.4\)      -42.5%           p < 0.001) Tj
T* (Transepidermal Water Loss \(TEWL\)    18.5 \(2.9\)          12.6 \(2.2\)        -31.9%           p < 0.01) Tj
T* (=================================================================================================) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Statistical Summary Narrative:) Tj
T* (At Day 14, subjects treated with Formula B-88 demonstrated a statistically significant) Tj
T* (94.2% hydration increase \(p < 0.001\), 68.0% acne lesion reduction \(p < 0.001\), and) Tj
T* (42.5% sebum reduction \(p < 0.001\) compared to baseline values across the N=120 cohort.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Regulatory Citation Reference:) Tj
T* (All advertising claims citing this trial must reference: Clinical Study CS-2026-88, Page 7, Table 2.1.) Tj
T* (Over-claims exceeding 94.2% hydration increase or promising results in less than 14 days) Tj
T* (are scientifically invalid and breach advertising substantiation standards.) Tj
T* () Tj
T* (Page 7 of 8) Tj
